        "text": "Describes how recommendations were formulated at two technical consultations in April and June 2012, the second on contraception only, and why recommendations on antiretroviral therapy were removed to align with newer WHO HIV guidance. It explains how the group weighed benefits and harms, and covers declarations of interest. It also notes that no recommendation was made on lay workers giving injectable contraceptives with prefilled devices pending a study, and describes document preparation and external peer review.",
